@startuml
skinparam dpi 110
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam wrapWidth 320
skinparam maxMessageSize 300
skinparam ArrowColor #1E293B
skinparam titleFontSize 20
skinparam titleFontStyle bold
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #F1F5F9
skinparam noteBorderColor #64748B
skinparam noteFontSize 12
skinparam legendBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam legendBorderColor #94A3B8
skinparam legendFontSize 12
skinparam sequence {
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
  ParticipantBorderColor #334155
  LifeLineBorderColor #94A3B8
  GroupBackgroundColor #F1F5F9
  GroupBorderColor #64748B
  DividerBackgroundColor #E2E8F0
}
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
title Ideator — sequence diagram (designed workflow, 2026-11-10)

actor "User\n(Ronni)" as U
participant "Ideator" as I
participant "Web / research\nsources" as W
participant "sheet_builder.py\n(local, /workspace/ideas)" as B
participant "Google Drive\nconnector" as D
database "Google Sheet\n(output)" as S
participant "Routine\nscheduler" as R

== Greeting (only when no problem statement) ==
U -> I : hi / opens chat
I --> U : intro + "Tip: give me a problem statement."\nRun knobs list with defaults (ideas 5, pretotypes 4,\nsources 5, country United States, language English,\nformat sheet, mode <saved or auto>,\ntemplate https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/15QQc1JBY3Vu7xxubbQRnX8BpTj8RtGDCjewJph-QFYA/edit)\n+ pretotype explanation + example problem

== Start ==
U -> I : problem statement [+ optional knobs]
I -> I : parse knobs (missing = default; never asked)\ncountry/language never from memory\nsave mode only; template per run\nrecord run_started (with seconds)
note right of I : no opening message before the run

== Discover ==
I -> W : web research (complaints, reviews, forums,\narticles, competitors) for the country market
W --> I : <sources> distinct sources
I -> I : challenges C1..C10 (cited, or\n"hypothesis, no evidence found") + sticky notes\nsave Sources / Sticky notes to run JSON

== Define ==
I -> I : Possible + Exciting (1-5 each) -> Score; rank\nties: Exciting > Possible > ID; top 5\nsave to JSON
alt mode = ask
  I -> U : PAUSE: ranked challenges, which to pursue?
  U --> I : chosen / steered challenges
else mode = auto
  I -> I : auto-pick top 5, record reason
end

== Develop ==
I -> I : <ideas> ideas per picked challenge,\nfitted to the country; save to JSON

== Deliver ==
I -> I : weighted = (Cheap + Simple) x evidence (1.3/1.15/1.0)\nx uniqueness (1.2/1.1/1.0), 1 decimal; top 5\nties: evidence > uniqueness > Simple > Cheap\n(else "unresolved tie, order arbitrary")\nconcepts ranked by avg weighted score; save to JSON
alt mode = ask
  I -> U : PAUSE: ranked ideas + concepts, which to pretotype?
  U --> I : chosen concepts
else mode = auto
  I -> I : auto-pick top 5 ideas, top 2 concepts
end

== Pretotypes ==
I -> I : <pretotypes> tests (hypothesis, success number,\ndeadline, go / no-go, recommended first test)\nmaterials drafted only, never sent; save to JSON
alt mode = ask
  I -> U : PAUSE: which tests will you run, and when?
  U --> I : selection [+ start dates]
else mode = auto
  I -> I : recommended first tests = selected;\ncheck-in waits for a start date
end

== Report build: build locally, upload once ==
I -> I : set run_stopped (with seconds) in run JSON
alt template set (default: Ideator Template)
  I -> D : export_file(template, xlsx) — once, read-only
  D --> I : template-export.xlsx
  I -> B : sheet_builder.py run.json --template template-export.xlsx
  B -> B : build 15 report tabs from scratch (row 1, no branding)\ntemplate's own tabs first, read-only (fingerprint assert)\nsame-named tabs replaced in place, others appended
  B --> I : <name>.xlsx + warnings
else template: none
  I -> B : sheet_builder.py run.json
  B --> I : <name>.xlsx (15 tabs from scratch)
end
I -> D : create_file(title = <problem>-YYYY-MM-DD-HHMM,\nxlsx base64, target = native Google Sheet) — ONE call
D -> S : create native Google Sheet in My Drive
D --> I : file id + link
I -> D : get_file_metadata (native sheet, run name)
opt name is not the run name (e.g. "Copy of ...")
  I -> D : update_file: rename the copy (never the template)
end
I -> D : get_file_permissions (owner only, never shared)
I -> D : export_file(new sheet, xlsx) — one compare
D --> I : xlsx
I -> I : compare locally with <name>.xlsx; fix real mismatches only
I --> U : final delivery (one message): problem verbatim,\nRun knobs (8 lines), "Here is the result.", sheet-name link

== Follow-up (later) ==
U -> I : start date(s) for selected tests
I -> R : create one-time routine: day after each deadline
R -> I : routine fires
I -> U : ask for results
U --> I : observed results
I -> I : compare with success number -> go / no-go / iterate\nupdate JSON, rebuild (same template branch)
I -> D : create_file new sheet named with update time
I --> U : which sheet is now current (older sheet kept)
I -> R : delete spent routine

== Cancellation (any time) ==
U -> I : cancel
I -> I : stop all work; Problem "Cancelled" = CANCELLED; rebuild
I -> D : create_file rebuilt sheet
I -> R : delete follow-up routine(s)

legend bottom
  Never delete anything on Drive. The template file is never written, renamed, moved, shared or deleted.
  If the Drive connector is missing: tell the user to connect Google Drive and stop; no other delivery.
endlegend
@enduml
